---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Header from '../../components/Header.astro';
import Footer from '../../components/Footer.astro';
import CTASection from '../../components/CTASection.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="How Much Does Painting Cost in Kissimmee? | Go Pro Guide"
  description="Honest painting cost ranges for Kissimmee & Central Florida. What drives price, what to expect, and how to get an accurate estimate from a local contractor."
  ogImage="/images/bedroom-paint.jpg"
  schema={{
    "@context": "https://schema.org",
    "@graph": [
      {
        "@type": "Article",
        "@id": "https://goprohomeimprovements.com/guides/how-much-does-painting-cost-kissimmee/#article",
        "headline": "How Much Does Painting Cost in Kissimmee?",
        "description": "Honest ranges for interior and exterior painting costs. What drives price and how to get an accurate estimate.",
        "author": {
          "@type": "Organization",
          "name": "GO PRO HOME IMPROVEMENTS INC."
        },
        "publisher": {
          "@type": "Organization",
          "name": "GO PRO HOME IMPROVEMENTS INC.",
          "logo": {
            "@type": "ImageObject",
            "url": "https://goprohomeimprovements.com/images/logo.png"
          }
        }
      },
      {
        "@type": "BreadcrumbList",
        "@id": "https://goprohomeimprovements.com/guides/how-much-does-painting-cost-kissimmee/#breadcrumbs",
        "itemListElement": [
          {
            "@type": "ListItem",
            "position": 1,
            "name": "Home",
            "item": "https://goprohomeimprovements.com"
          },
          {
            "@type": "ListItem",
            "position": 2,
            "name": "Guides",
            "item": "https://goprohomeimprovements.com/guides"
          },
          {
            "@type": "ListItem",
            "position": 3,
            "name": "Painting Costs",
            "item": "https://goprohomeimprovements.com/guides/how-much-does-painting-cost-kissimmee"
          }
        ]
      }
    ]
  }}
>
  <Header />

  <section class="bg-gopro-charcoal text-white py-16 border-b-4 border-gopro-orange">
    <div class="container-custom">
      <nav class="text-sm mb-6 font-sans">
        <a href="/" class="text-gray-400 hover:text-gopro-orange transition-colors">Home</a>
        <span class="mx-2 text-gray-500">/</span>
        <a href="/guides" class="text-gray-400 hover:text-gopro-orange transition-colors">Guides</a>
        <span class="mx-2 text-gray-500">/</span>
        <span class="text-white">Painting Costs</span>
      </nav>
      <h1 class="text-4xl md:text-5xl font-display font-black uppercase mb-4 tracking-tight">How Much Does Painting Cost in Kissimmee?</h1>
      <p class="text-xl text-gray-300 max-w-3xl font-sans">
        Honest ranges for interior and exterior painting. What drives price, what to expect, and how to get an accurate estimate.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section-padding">
    <div class="container-custom">
      <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto">
        <div class="prose prose-lg max-w-none">
          <p class="text-xl text-gray-700 leading-relaxed mb-6 font-sans">
            "How much does painting cost?" is the first question every homeowner asks. The answer is always "it depends"—but here's what it depends on, with real ranges from 15+ years of <a href="/services/interior-exterior-painting" class="text-gopro-orange hover:underline">painting</a> in <a href="/areas/kissimmee" class="text-gopro-orange hover:underline">Kissimmee</a>, <a href="/areas/orlando" class="text-gopro-orange hover:underline">Orlando</a>, and Central Florida.
          </p>

          <h2 class="text-3xl font-display font-black uppercase mb-6 tracking-tight mt-12">Interior Painting Costs</h2>
          
          <h3 class="text-2xl font-display font-bold uppercase mb-4 tracking-wide mt-8">Single Room</h3>
          <ul class="list-none space-y-2 mb-6 text-gray-700 font-sans">
            <li><strong>Small bedroom (10x12):</strong> $300-$500</li>
            <li><strong>Large bedroom (12x15):</strong> $400-$650</li>
            <li><strong>Living room (15x18):</strong> $500-$900</li>
            <li><strong>Kitchen or bathroom:</strong> $350-$600</li>
          </ul>
          <p class="text-lg text-gray-700 mb-6 font-sans">
            Includes ceiling, walls, <a href="/services/trim-crown-molding" class="text-gopro-orange hover:underline">trim</a>, prep work (patching, sanding), two coats of paint, and cleanup. If the walls are dark and you're going lighter, add a coat of primer ($100-$200 extra).
          </p>

          <h3 class="text-2xl font-display font-bold uppercase mb-4 tracking-wide mt-8">Whole House Interior</h3>
          <ul class="list-none space-y-2 mb-6 text-gray-700 font-sans">
            <li><strong>Small house (1,200-1,500 sq ft):</strong> $2,500-$4,500</li>
            <li><strong>Medium house (1,800-2,200 sq ft):</strong> $4,000-$6,500</li>
            <li><strong>Large house (2,500-3,500 sq ft):</strong> $6,000-$10,000</li>
          </ul>
          <p class="text-lg text-gray-700 mb-6 font-sans">
            Full interior includes all walls, ceilings, trim, closets, and hallways. Price depends on ceiling height, number of rooms, surface condition, and color changes. Vaulted ceilings, heavy texture, or extensive <a href="/services/drywall" class="text-gopro-orange hover:underline">drywall</a> repairs add cost.
          </p>

          <h2 class="text-3xl font-display font-black uppercase mb-6 tracking-tight mt-12">Exterior Painting Costs</h2>
          
          <h3 class="text-2xl font-display font-bold uppercase mb-4 tracking-wide mt-8">Full Exterior</h3>
          <ul class="list-none space-y-2 mb-6 text-gray-700 font-sans">
            <li><strong>Small house (1,000-1,500 sq ft):</strong> $2,500-$4,500</li>
            <li><strong>Medium house (1,500-2,500 sq ft):</strong> $4,000-$7,000</li>
            <li><strong>Large house (2,500-3,500 sq ft):</strong> $6,500-$12,000</li>
          </ul>
          <p class="text-lg text-gray-700 mb-6 font-sans">
            Includes <a href="/services/power-washing" class="text-gopro-orange hover:underline">power washing</a>, scraping loose paint, priming bare wood or stucco, two coats of quality exterior paint, and painting trim. Florida sun and humidity demand good prep—if we skip the wash or rush dry time, paint peels early.
          </p>

          <h3 class="text-2xl font-display font-bold uppercase mb-4 tracking-wide mt-8">Trim, Doors & Shutters Only</h3>
          <ul class="list-none space-y-2 mb-6 text-gray-700 font-sans">
            <li><strong>Trim only:</strong> $800-$1,800</li>
            <li><strong>Front door:</strong> $150-$350</li>
            <li><strong>Shutters (per pair):</strong> $100-$200</li>
          </ul>
          <p class="text-lg text-gray-700 mb-6 font-sans">
            Many Kissimmee and Orlando homeowners refresh just the trim, front door, and shutters to boost curb appeal before selling. Costs less than a full exterior repaint and makes a big visual difference in photos.
          </p>

          <h2 class="text-3xl font-display font-black uppercase mb-6 tracking-tight mt-12">What Drives Painting Cost?</h2>
          
          <h3 class="text-2xl font-display font-bold uppercase mb-4 tracking-wide mt-8">1. Surface Area & Ceiling Height</h3>
          <p class="text-lg text-gray-700 mb-6 font-sans">
            More square footage = more paint and more labor. Standard 8-foot ceilings are baseline. 10-foot ceilings cost 15-20% more. Vaulted or cathedral ceilings double the cost because they're harder to reach and take longer.
          </p>

          <h3 class="text-2xl font-display font-bold uppercase mb-4 tracking-wide mt-8">2. Surface Condition</h3>
          <p class="text-lg text-gray-700 mb-6 font-sans">
            Smooth walls in good condition paint fast. Walls with holes, cracks, heavy texture, or water stains need <a href="/services/drywall" class="text-gopro-orange hover:underline">patching and sanding</a> first. Exterior wood rot, peeling stucco, or mildew-covered siding add prep time. More prep = higher cost.
          </p>

          <h3 class="text-2xl font-display font-bold uppercase mb-4 tracking-wide mt-8">3. Color Changes</h3>
          <p class="text-lg text-gray-700 mb-6 font-sans">
            Painting over the same or similar color is two coats. Going from dark to light (navy to white, for example) needs primer plus two coats. That's an extra $150-$400 per room.
          </p>

          <h3 class="text-2xl font-display font-bold uppercase mb-4 tracking-wide mt-8">4. Paint Quality</h3>
          <p class="text-lg text-gray-700 mb-6 font-sans">
            Contractor-grade paint (Sherwin-Williams, Benjamin Moore, Behr Premium) costs $40-$70 per gallon. Budget paint is $25-$35 but requires more coats and doesn't last. Exterior paint needs UV and mildew resistance for Florida—cheap paint fades and mildews in two years.
          </p>

          <div class="bg-gopro-orange/10 border-l-4 border-gopro-orange p-6 my-8">
            <p class="text-gray-700 font-sans mb-0">
              <strong>Our take:</strong> We use quality paint rated for Florida's climate. It costs a bit more upfront but lasts 5-7 years instead of 2-3. Repainting every few years because you went cheap the first time costs more long-term.
            </p>
          </div>

          <h3 class="text-2xl font-display font-bold uppercase mb-4 tracking-wide mt-8">5. Trim & Detail Work</h3>
          <p class="text-lg text-gray-700 mb-6 font-sans">
            Painting trim, crown molding, baseboards, doors, and window frames takes time. Homes with lots of trim cost more than homes with minimal trim. If you want trim painted a different color than walls (white trim, colored walls), that's extra masking and cutting-in.
          </p>

          <h2 class="text-3xl font-display font-black uppercase mb-6 tracking-tight mt-12">What's Included in a Painting Estimate?</h2>
          <p class="text-lg text-gray-700 mb-6 font-sans">
            A complete painting estimate should include:
          </p>
          <ul class="list-disc pl-6 mb-6 space-y-2 text-gray-700 font-sans">
            <li>Labor (prep, priming, painting, cleanup)</li>
            <li>Materials (paint, primer, tape, drop cloths)</li>
            <li>Surface prep (patching, sanding, caulking)</li>
            <li>Power washing (exterior jobs)</li>
            <li>Number of coats</li>
            <li>What's being painted (walls, ceiling, trim, doors)</li>
          </ul>
          <p class="text-lg text-gray-700 mb-6 font-sans">
            If an estimate just says "paint house $3,000," ask for details. You need to know what's included so you can compare apples to apples when shopping contractors.
          </p>

          <h2 class="text-3xl font-display font-black uppercase mb-6 tracking-tight mt-12">How to Get an Accurate Estimate</h2>
          <p class="text-lg text-gray-700 mb-6 font-sans">
            No contractor can give you an exact price over the phone. They need to see the house, measure rooms, check surface condition, and ask about colors and trim. A real estimate takes 20-30 minutes on-site.
          </p>
          <p class="text-lg text-gray-700 mb-6 font-sans">
            We do <a href="/estimate" class="text-gopro-orange hover:underline">free estimates</a> in <a href="/areas/kissimmee" class="text-gopro-orange hover:underline">Kissimmee</a>, <a href="/areas/orlando" class="text-gopro-orange hover:underline">Orlando</a>, <a href="/areas/celebration" class="text-gopro-orange hover:underline">Celebration</a>, <a href="/areas/st-cloud" class="text-gopro-orange hover:underline">St. Cloud</a>, and <a href="/areas/poinciana" class="text-gopro-orange hover:underline">Poinciana</a>. We walk the property, measure, ask what you want painted, and give you a written quote with all costs itemized. No surprises.
          </p>

          <h2 class="text-3xl font-display font-black uppercase mb-6 tracking-tight mt-12">Common Questions</h2>
          
          <div class="space-y-6 my-8">
            <div class="bg-white border-l-4 border-gopro-orange p-6">
              <h3 class="text-xl font-display font-bold uppercase mb-2 tracking-wide">Should I supply the paint or does the contractor?</h3>
              <p class="text-gray-700 font-sans mb-0">
                Most contractors (us included) supply the paint. We buy at contractor pricing and know which products hold up in Florida. If you already bought paint, let us know—we'll use it, but we can't warranty the finish if the paint fails.
              </p>
            </div>
            <div class="bg-white border-l-4 border-gopro-orange p-6">
              <h3 class="text-xl font-display font-bold uppercase mb-2 tracking-wide">Does painting include moving furniture?</h3>
              <p class="text-gray-700 font-sans mb-0">
                We move small furniture (chairs, lamps, decor) away from walls and cover it. Heavy furniture (beds, dressers, couches) we work around. If you need help moving big pieces, let us know before the job starts.
              </p>
            </div>
            <div class="bg-white border-l-4 border-gopro-orange p-6">
              <h3 class="text-xl font-display font-bold uppercase mb-2 tracking-wide">How long does painting take?</h3>
              <p class="text-gray-700 font-sans mb-0">
                Single room: 1 day. Whole house interior: 3-7 days depending on size. Exterior: 3-5 days including power wash dry time. We give you a schedule upfront so you know when we'll be there.
              </p>
            </div>
            <div class="bg-white border-l-4 border-gopro-orange p-6">
              <h3 class="text-xl font-display font-bold uppercase mb-2 tracking-wide">Why do some quotes seem really cheap?</h3>
              <p class="text-gray-700 font-sans mb-0">
                If a quote is way below market, the contractor is either skipping prep, using cheap paint, rushing the job, or planning to upsell you mid-project. Quality painting isn't the cheapest—but it's not the most expensive either. Look for fair pricing + experience + clear scope.
              </p>
            </div>
          </div>

          <h2 class="text-3xl font-display font-black uppercase mb-6 tracking-tight mt-12">The Bottom Line</h2>
          <p class="text-lg text-gray-700 mb-6 font-sans">
            Interior painting costs $300-$900 per room or $2,500-$10,000 for a whole house. Exterior painting costs $2,500-$12,000 depending on size and condition. What drives price: square footage, ceiling height, surface condition, color changes, and trim work. Get an on-site estimate so you know exactly what you're paying for—no surprises.
          </p>

          <div class="bg-gray-50 rounded-lg p-8 my-8">
            <h3 class="text-2xl font-display font-bold uppercase mb-4 tracking-wide">Need a Painting Estimate?</h3>
            <p class="text-gray-700 font-sans mb-6">
              We provide free, detailed estimates in Kissimmee, Orlando, and Central Florida. On-site measurement, itemized quote, and no pressure. Call or request online.
            </p>
            <div class="flex flex-col sm:flex-row gap-4">
              <a href="/estimate" class="btn-primary">
                Get Free Estimate
              </a>
              <a href="tel:4072446873" class="btn-secondary">
                Call (407) 244-6873
              </a>
            </div>
          </div>

          <div class="mt-12 pt-8 border-t border-gray-200">
            <p class="text-sm text-gray-600 font-sans">
              <a href="/guides" class="text-gopro-orange hover:underline">← Back to All Guides</a>
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <CTASection
    title="Ready to Paint Your Home?"
    description="Free estimates, quality work, and honest pricing. Serving Kissimmee, Orlando & Central Florida."
  />

  <Footer />
</BaseLayout>
